{% decision_card number="ADR-0007" status="approved" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

Provider switching, policy, evidence, and completion cannot safely live inside ad hoc prompts or Astro pages.

## Decision drivers

- Provider neutrality
- Policy enforcement
- Continuation
- Auditability
- No self-completion

## Options considered

- Direct page-to-provider calls
- Prompt-only routing
- Separate internal orchestration module

## Decision

Implement a separate in-repository broker module as an in-memory simulation. Durable service extraction and live invocation remain future decisions.

## Positive consequences

- Explicit testable boundaries
- Pages do not own routing policy

## Negative consequences

- Simulation is not operational automation

## Risks

- Users may mistake prompt previews for live work

## Follow-up work

- Keep simulated labels visible
- Require a new ADR before a live or external broker

## Supersedes or superseded by

Supersedes ADR-0004’s blanket no-broker clause while preserving file-based continuity.

